userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: In an Ames room, a trapezoidal floor plan viewed through a single pinhole produces the same visual angles as a rectangular room, so the brain mislocalizes objects along their sight lines and misjudges their sizes.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A single pinhole measures only angles, never depth — so a trapezoidal room and a rectangular room can cast identical images, and the brain's rectangular assumption converts an error in assumed depth into an error in perceived size.
DEMO STEPS: 7 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
